WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:05.740
Todd Phillips, the director of the upcoming
Joker movie has publicly revealed the first

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.340
official look at Joaquin Phoenix in the lead
role.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:12.480
The surprisingly-stripped down image was posted
to Phillips' Instagram page with the one-word

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.860
caption, "Arthur."

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.040
Without the context of the upcoming solo movie,
you'd never know this was supposed to be a

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.180
portrait of the Clown Prince of Crime.

00:00:20.429 --> 00:00:24.980
Save for a greasy hairstyle and a few extra
wrinkles, Phoenix looks a lot like himself

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.900
in the photo - but there's a reason for that.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.880
Phillips, who has directed films like Old
School, Starsky &amp; Hutch, and the three movies

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.840
of The Hangover series, isn't making a movie
about the Joker at the height of his powers.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:40.020
Instead, Joker is expected to be a dark and
experimental story, reportedly centering around

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.700
a failed comedian in the 1980s, who snaps
and transitions to a legendary life of crime.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.460
Phoenix is playing the Joker as an everyday
guy, and this glimpse appears to be from just

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.940
before his one bad day sends him over the
edge.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.199
With that in mind, it makes sense that the
first reveal of Phoenix in character doesn't

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.220
feature him in the typical Joker look.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.820
Here he's just a fairly normal dude, struggling
to realize his dream of making people laugh.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.640
When he comes to terms with the fact that
his career may never take off, he takes matters

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.520
into his own hands in a decidedly theatrical
way.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.060
It sounds pretty relatable, aside from the
whole "domestic terrorism" thing.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.980
Phillips' big reveal seems to confirm a previous
report by That Hashtag Show that stirred up

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:20.900
a ton of hype.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.940
In July, the outlet posted an article claiming
that the Joker's real name in the movie would

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.660
be revealed as Arthur Fleck.

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:31.340
Now that Phillips himself has mentioned the
name, it seems a sure bet that Mr. Fleck is

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.340
our leading man.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:36.720
In the same write-up, That Hashtag Show also
reported that the Joker movie will see Arthur

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:41.200
moving in with his sick mother, Penny, and
later meeting a woman named Sophie Dumond,

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.540
who may be played by Zazie Beetz of Atlanta
and Deadpool 2.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.420
Other reports would seem to corroborate those
details.

00:01:47.689 --> 00:01:52.340
The outlet's most outlandish hypothesis, that
the Joker and the Batman will be revealed

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.399
to be half-brothers, has yet to be confirmed
or denied.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:00.260
But we do know that Batman's father, Thomas
Wayne, will be a part of the movie - so perhaps

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.540
there's some truth to that tidbit as well.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.180
A major part of the Joker's appeal over the
years has been his generally-unknown, constantly

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.440
shifting origins.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:14.040
Aside from the 1989 Batman movie, which presented
the character as a gangster named Jack Napier,

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.160
the Joker typically hasn't been shown as having
a traditional backstory.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.800
He's usually more of an agent of chaos with
a contradictory history that he routinely

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:22.500
lies about.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.380
"Ya wanna know how I got these scars?"

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.620
Despite that history of ambiguity, the fact
that this movie appears to be nailing down

00:02:29.629 --> 00:02:33.420
one origin story for the Joker isn't anything
to be alarmed about.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.580
It's not meant to be a definitive interpretation
- just a different one.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:41.200
The Fox series Gotham, a prequel-of-sorts
to the world of Batman, has also spent the

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:47.129
last few years playing around with the Joker-inspired
characters Jerome and Jeremiah Valeska - unhinged

00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:51.440
villains who have frequently been teased as
potentially being younger versions of the

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.100
Joker we know.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:56.560
But what's true in the world of Gotham doesn't
need to be true for any other Batman story,

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.180
and the same goes for this solo movie.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:03.460
Unlike the shared universe occupied by movies
like Suicide Squad, Wonder Woman, and Justice

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:08.500
League, Joaquin Phoenix's Joker movie is set
to be a standalone film, existing outside

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.880
of established continuity to tell a radically
different story.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.700
It's a new approach for DC Comics on screen.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:19.440
And if it works out, we can probably expect
other alternate universe, Elseworlds-type

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.240
stories to follow - like the Soviet Union
Superman story, Superman: Red Son.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:29.660
This alternate universe aspect is a big part
of what makes Joker so potentially special.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:34.069
It gives Phillips and Phoenix the freedom
to be weird and take chances without worrying

00:03:34.069 --> 00:03:37.460
about sequels, spinoffs, or what's going on
in the Batman movies.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.740
It's a great first look at one of 2019's most
curious projects, and we can't wait to find

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:43.240
out more.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.840
"You…

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.920
You just couldn't let me go, could you?"

